<title>MOROCCO: EU grants emergency aid for Moroccan flood victims.</title>
<headline>EU grants emergency aid for Moroccan flood victims.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Wednesday said it granted emergency aid of 300,000 EcuS ($375,000) to Morocco to help about 6,000 families affected by floods.</p>
<p>In a statement issued in Rabat it said the aid for around 30,000 people would help provide basic items like flour, oil, sugar and tea, and blankets.</p>
<p>Heavy rains have lashed much of Morocco for the past month, directly killing six people and destroying 43 houses, according to Interior Minister Driss Basri late last month.</p>
<p>Earlier this week, 23 people aboard a bus were swept away by floods. No trace has been reported of them.</p>
</text>
